WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:04.850
Kaito’s minion Jin kidnapped
Kotori and my friends!

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:08.290
Furthermore, he can see my cards!

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:11.200
If I lose, everyone’s lives are in danger!

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.700
I can’t give up!

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:14.570
I’m kattobing!

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:20.450
Kneel before Master Kaito!

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.790
I end my turn!

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.260
Kotori! Everyone!

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:36.800
Yuma...

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:40.640
I promise to rescue you.

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:44.190
Please save everyone.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.470
I’m afraid.

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:52.190
Why?

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:58.350
I felt death for the first time during that duel.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:02.380
I see. That was fear.

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:05.160
Astral! Hey, Astral!

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.520
Stop daydreaming!

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.840
If you don’t want to battle, then go away!

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:13.550
Yuma, you have zero monsters in your hand.

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:17.010
Due to Shock Master’s effect, you can’t use traps.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:22.430
If you don’t draw a monster
card this time, we’ll lose.

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:26.100
Then all I have to do is draw a monster!

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:29.110
My turn! I draw!

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:31.570
All right! It’s a monster card!

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:36.030
Kurivolt? It only has 300 ATK!

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:37.960
This monster is...

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:41.550
Yuma, summon Kurivolt!

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:43.760
This weak monster?

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:45.560
Just summon it.

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:47.370
Fine.

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:50.130
I summon Kurivolt!

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:58.600
Good.

00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:06.560
Kurivolt uses an Overlay Unit on the field to Special Summon a Kurivolt Token on to your field.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:11.270
Shock Master’s two Overlay Units
are currently on the field.

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:13.020
I see!

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:15.230
I activate Kurivolt’s effect!

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:20.170
I steal Shock Master’s two
Overlay Units to gain Kurivolts!

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:23.910
All right!

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:32.670
Awesome!

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:35.130
Now I have three Kurivolts!

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:39.130
That’s a very powerful effect.

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:42.350
But what can you do with three weaklings?

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:44.630
I can see it.

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:48.690
There are zero monster cards in your hand!

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:53.650
You can’t summon a stronger monster!

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:55.790
Don’t panic, Yuma.

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:57.530
Use Voltage Summon.

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:58.110
Right!

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:02.110
I activate the spell card Voltage Summon!

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:13.710
By tributing all your Kurivolt Tokens, you can Special Summon the same number of Level 4-or-below monsters from your deck.

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:14.840
I see!

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:17.560
I tribute two Kurivolt Tokens.

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:23.050
I Special Summon Ganbara Knight
and Kagetokage from my deck!

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:30.700
However, the monsters Special Summoned by this effect have 0 attack and DEF!

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:35.480
I overlay Level 4 Kagetokage and Ganbara Knight!

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:40.540
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:42.250
Xyz Summon!

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:48.490
Appear, Number 39: Utopia!

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:59.880
Despite the circumstances, Yuma managed to draw Kurivolt and successfully summon Utopia with his combo.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:01.570
You’re incredible.

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:06.510
So that’s your Number.

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:08.890
Go, Utopia!

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:11.980
Attack Shock Master!

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:14.560
Hope Sword Slash!

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.990
All right! I destroyed his Number!

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.250
I still have another attack!

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:31.910
Kurivolt attacks you directly!

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:43.090
Everyone, just wait! I’ll rescue you!

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:44.770
I’ll now end my tur—

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:45.740
Wait.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:48.120
Set the traps in your hand.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:51.810
You can’t use a trap yet, but you can have it ready.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.480
I understand!

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:56.590
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:04:57.390 --> 00:05:01.630
There still may be hope.

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:09.130
What’s so funny?

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:10.760
Don’t get overconfident!

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:14.180
I’ll make you feel even more pain!

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:21.340
Whether it’s rain, wind, blizzard or the scorching sun

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:23.970
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:27.430
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:31.590
Freedom begins by accepting differences Dance and create the universe

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:39.400
In truth, I was sad until I met you

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:45.640
I lied, thinking it was easier to be alone

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:52.070
Even though we don’t like the same books or hobbies

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:55.940
You’re the only one who agreed with me

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:58.790
Joy and sadness and anger and do re mi fa so la ti do

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:00.540
There’s no harmony and scenario without differences

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:04.510
Everyone is not the same

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:08.680
That’s the reason for living

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:14.850
Even if the sounds are dissonant at times

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:19.840
That’s why I never give up
I believe my strength will get me through

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:23.520
I travel to the edge of the world

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:27.990
The sights I see with you are the truth

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:30.840
Whether it’s rain, wind, blizzard or the scorching sun

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:34.080
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:36.980
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:41.130
Freedom begins by accepting differences Dance and create the universe

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:48.510
My turn! I draw!

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:52.720
\hChaos Xyz Change! The Light of Hope, Utopia Ray!!\h

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:52.720
Number 18:

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:52.720
I Special Summon Rainbow Shaman from my hand.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:07:01.690
I can Special Summon it from my hand when I have no monsters on my field and you have a Xyz Monster on your field!

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:04.320
Level 7? Are you serious?

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.190
But it has 0 ATK.

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:13.970
Next, I select Rainbow Shaman and activate the Continuous Spell Xyz Plant!

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:21.770
The Continuous Spell Xyz Plant is Special Summoned as a monster with 0 ATK.

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:25.630
It has the same Level as Rainbow Shaman, so it’s Level 7.

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:28.090
A spell card transforms into a monster?

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:29.590
Can it be?

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:34.300
I overlay Level 7 Rainbow Shaman and Xyz Plant!

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:43.260
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network.

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:47.980
Xyz Summon! Appear, Number 11!

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:54.660
The ruler with the bewitching eye! Big Eye!

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:02.420
No way! A second Number?

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:04.420
And it’s Rank 7.

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:11.220
You thought that I only used one Number?

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:16.850
I have a power that rivals Kaito’s!

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:24.740
Can Yuma really beat him?

00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:26.770
To summarize, he’s too strong.

00:08:27.140 --> 00:08:29.250
Let’s trust Yuma.

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:34.410
Yuma, don’t panic. You have Utopia’s effect.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:35.950
I know!

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:39.950
Utopia can negate an attack by using an Overlay Unit.

00:08:40.550 --> 00:08:43.910
Even if it’s Rank 7, the attack won’t succeed!

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:49.250
I activate Big Eye’s effect!

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:56.610
By using one Overlay Unit, Big Eye takes control of one of your monsters!

00:08:57.390 --> 00:09:01.870
Your Number Utopia is mine!

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:03.310
What?

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:07.620
Do it, Big Eye! Temptation Glance!

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:16.070
Oh no! My Utopia!

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:18.530
This is the strength of a Rank 7.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:22.040
It can control any monster.

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:28.250
Utopia, attack Kurivolt for me!

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:43.350
I’m going to fall!

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:45.100
Save me!

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:49.770
When Big Eye uses an Xyz Effect,
it can’t attack that turn.

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:53.270
Be afraid of death!

00:09:55.700 --> 00:09:59.700
I set one card and end my turn.

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:03.450
It’s not over!

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:06.000
My turn! I draw!

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:07.210
Here it is!

00:10:07.770 --> 00:10:10.210
I can now summon a monster!

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:15.670
Did you forget that I can see all your cards?

00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:16.840
What?

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:22.300
You drew a monster card.

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:26.020
I activate the Continuous Trap Freezing Dance!

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:36.400
Both players can’t summon, Special Summon or set a monster from their hands for the next two turns.

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:41.040
Yuma can’t summon a monster,
so he’ll take his attack!

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:41.870
Oh no!

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:45.160
I end my turn.

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:48.120
My turn! I draw!

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:52.330
This is the end.

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:55.500
Fall into the depths of hell with your friends!

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:56.550
Battle!

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:59.010
Big Eye attacks you directly!

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:00.890
Use the trap card, Yuma!

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:02.390
Oh yeah!

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:05.010
Starting this turn, I can use traps again!

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:07.470
I activate the trap Nitwit Outwit!

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:11.000
When your monster attacks me directly...

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:18.090
I send one monster card in my hand to the graveyard, and the battle damage decreases by its ATK!

00:11:19.350 --> 00:11:22.660
Dododo Warrior, protect us!

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:34.890
You haven’t escaped death yet!

00:11:34.890 --> 00:11:36.380
Take this!

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:39.130
Utopia attacks you directly!

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:41.590
Yuma, use the other trap!

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:45.350
Right! I activate the trap Xyz Weight!

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:53.390
An Xyz Monster loses 800 ATK
for every Overlay Unit it has!

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:00.400
Yuma!

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:15.510
Kotori...

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:21.270
You managed to survive two monster attacks.

00:12:21.270 --> 00:12:26.050
In that case, I activate the Continuous Spell Twilight Dance!

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:30.980
Both players can’t Special Summon
monsters from their graveyards!

00:12:35.030 --> 00:12:37.650
Now you can’t do anything.

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:38.900
Yuma...

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:41.360
You have no monsters on your field.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:45.770
But I have two powerful monsters on my field!

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:48.800
You can’t fight back anymore!

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:52.080
You and your friends’ lives are over next turn!

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:55.280
I end my turn!

00:12:57.750 --> 00:12:59.120
Damn...

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:05.690
This is the end.

00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:09.680
Everyone...

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:17.310
There’s only one way to save your friends.

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:22.130
Surrender from this duel.

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:26.280
Accept defeat and hand over all your Numbers.

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:30.280
If you do, I’ll let your friends live.

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:31.700
What?

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:36.210
It’s a good exchange.

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:40.690
Only one person needs to be sacrificed to save all your friends.

00:13:43.330 --> 00:13:45.520
Save me!

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:46.720
Yuma!

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:49.350
Don’t do it!

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:51.760
Yuma!

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:57.020
How entertaining!

00:13:57.430 --> 00:14:00.730
Cry, scream and suffer!

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:11.320
We shouldn’t have battled.

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:15.590
Victory is close to zero.

00:14:15.590 --> 00:14:19.630
Even if we continue the duel, you can’t save your friends.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:23.590
We only have one option.

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:28.050
Hand over the Number Cards.

00:14:28.810 --> 00:14:30.480
You...

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:35.520
We’ll vanish together.

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:37.820
Surrender.

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:43.400
Stop joking!

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:45.680
Yuma?

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:48.110
I met a lot of people through dueling.

00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:57.580
I lost now and then, but everyone I dueled with are my dear friends!

00:14:58.250 --> 00:15:03.940
I won’t abandon a single friend!

00:15:03.940 --> 00:15:06.670
Yuma, that’s why I—

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:08.640
You still don’t understand?

00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:14.600
You’re my dear friend, Astral!

00:15:22.700 --> 00:15:23.940
Astral...

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:25.560
Yuma...

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:27.660
Hey, kid!

00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:30.950
Hurry up and surrender
and hand over your Numbers!

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:36.900
Whatever! I’ll never surrender!

00:15:36.900 --> 00:15:38.640
Fine.

00:15:38.640 --> 00:15:43.890
Kaito is looking forward to
seeing you lose your soul.

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:48.780
Hey, Kaito!

00:15:48.780 --> 00:15:50.970
Is he really your minion?

00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:54.680
Is your dueling the same as his?

00:15:56.630 --> 00:16:00.180
Is that really Kaito up there?

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:02.570
What are you saying?

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:05.560
Can it be?

00:16:09.310 --> 00:16:11.850
I’m cattabing!

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:23.710
A mannequin?

00:16:24.150 --> 00:16:26.670
What’s going on?

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:30.170
It can’t be... My master Kaito is...

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:31.960
Just like I thought!

00:16:31.960 --> 00:16:33.880
I’ve dueled against Kaito.

00:16:34.440 --> 00:16:42.770
He’s scary strong, but he doesn’t enjoy watching people suffer while dueling!

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:45.980
He’s not garbage like you!

00:16:50.020 --> 00:16:54.690
I was afraid of that?

00:16:55.790 --> 00:16:57.320
I was scared too.

00:16:57.750 --> 00:17:01.750
But there’s always hope
as long as you don’t give up!

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:03.760
Kattobing!

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:04.710
Yuma...

00:17:05.800 --> 00:17:06.920
I see.

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:11.630
Fear wasn’t the only new emotion I felt.

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:14.760
You gave me another important emotion.

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:16.680
Yuma...

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:24.640
I want to win for you and your friends!

00:17:31.430 --> 00:17:32.650
You’re...

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:34.610
What?

00:17:39.400 --> 00:17:40.780
That’s...

00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:43.540
Astral...

00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:48.250
Let’s win, Yuma.

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:50.710
Astral, let’s go!

00:17:51.270 --> 00:17:52.800
My turn!

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:54.920
I draw!

00:17:55.480 --> 00:17:57.380
The spell card Comeback!

00:17:57.380 --> 00:18:00.100
Get Utopia back with that card!

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:01.680
All right!

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:05.390
I activate the spell card Comeback!

00:18:05.860 --> 00:18:10.030
I regain control of my stolen monster!

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:16.190
Come back, Utopia!

00:18:16.190 --> 00:18:17.150
What?

00:18:25.010 --> 00:18:29.870
We’ve assembled the new formula for victory!

00:18:29.870 --> 00:18:31.130
What’s this?

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:33.180
The power of hope.

00:18:33.180 --> 00:18:35.350
The messenger who changes chaos into light.

00:18:35.350 --> 00:18:37.050
Chaos Number 39.

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:38.760
Chaos Number?

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:45.270
Utopia and an Overlay Unit become one to further evolve!

00:18:45.920 --> 00:18:47.570
Let’s go, Yuma!

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:50.650
Chaos Xyz Change!

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:55.480
Appear now, Number C39!

00:18:57.880 --> 00:18:59.950
Utopia Ray!

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:18.920
What’s that?

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:19.760
Incredible!

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:21.720
Chaos Number?

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:26.230
My Big Eye is stronger,
so it won’t be destroyed!

00:19:26.230 --> 00:19:28.680
Utopia Ray’s effect activates!

00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:37.420
Utopia Ray can use
an Overlay Unit to gain 500 ATK!

00:19:43.390 --> 00:19:47.160
I use all three Overlay Units!

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:50.420
Utopia Ray gains ATK!

00:19:50.420 --> 00:19:52.400
Overlay Charge!

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:56.340
What?

00:19:56.340 --> 00:20:02.760
And your monster loses 1000 ATK
for every Overlay Unit!

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:04.220
No way!

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:07.720
Go, Utopia Ray!

00:20:08.210 --> 00:20:10.890
Attack Big Eye!

00:20:12.450 --> 00:20:16.560
Hope Sword Chaos Slash!

00:20:38.050 --> 00:20:39.590
Huh?

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:48.890
Yuma!

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:51.020
You’re safe!

00:20:51.760 --> 00:20:54.480
You’re incredible, Astral!

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:56.090
Thank you, Astral!

00:20:56.090 --> 00:20:57.390
You were incredible!

00:20:57.390 --> 00:20:59.690
Starting today, we’re friends!

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:03.630
Why are you focusing on Astral?

00:21:03.630 --> 00:21:06.450
I saved you!

00:21:06.450 --> 00:21:08.910
I’m disappointed!

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:11.120
Yuma! Wait!

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:17.550
Observation #13: As long as you have friends, you can believe in hope.

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:24.360
Yuma, thank you
for acknowledging me as a friend.

00:21:30.800 --> 00:21:33.230
Those fools.

00:21:34.140 --> 00:21:40.010
They didn’t know I had another Number.

00:21:41.980 --> 00:21:42.780
It’s you!

00:21:43.230 --> 00:21:46.740
Are you Kaito?

00:21:46.740 --> 00:21:51.080
Kaito, I worship you as a god!

00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:53.790
Let me be your minion.

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:54.850
I see.

00:21:54.850 --> 00:21:59.990
I’ll hunt your Number, along with your soul.

00:22:05.510 --> 00:22:08.340
Number retrieval complete.

00:22:12.890 --> 00:22:15.570
Let’s start the duel!

00:22:15.570 --> 00:22:17.570
This week’s quiz:

00:22:17.570 --> 00:22:22.710
To summon a high-Level monster, do you send the monster on the field to the graveyard?

00:22:22.710 --> 00:22:24.860
Or do you put it back in your hand?

00:22:30.590 --> 00:22:35.190
Today’s test is hard
Can’t avoid pleasure and temptation

00:22:35.190 --> 00:22:39.960
I want to go home and watch TV
Recent cartoons are entertaining

00:22:50.280 --> 00:22:54.770
Anyway, tests are hard
Language, math and English are especially hard

00:22:54.770 --> 00:22:59.560
Average scores in science and social studies
I’m only good at P.E.

00:22:59.950 --> 00:23:02.650
(Wait, Baby!) The expected

00:23:02.650 --> 00:23:04.860
(What’s that, Baby!) Answers

00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:07.650
(Wait a sec, Baby!) Remember them

00:23:07.650 --> 00:23:08.900
(What are we!? Baby!) For who

00:23:09.320 --> 00:23:13.960
Let’s say I wrote the correct answers on that sheet

00:23:13.960 --> 00:23:18.160
Will that change the future a year or a decade from now?

00:23:18.810 --> 00:23:23.870
The world I drew at the edge of dreams

00:23:23.870 --> 00:23:28.170
Someday I’ll race in the sky

00:23:28.640 --> 00:23:33.390
Nobody can threaten my heart

00:23:33.390 --> 00:23:37.460
Nothing is correct!

00:23:41.070 --> 00:23:43.960
This is a story from when Yuma
was still young.

00:23:43.960 --> 00:23:47.700
Memories of his parents,
the secret of the King’s Key, and...

00:23:47.700 --> 00:23:50.650
They don’t need to attend
the school’s open house!

00:23:50.650 --> 00:23:54.870
Is there a connection between me
and your father’s King’s Key?

00:23:54.870 --> 00:23:57.240
My dad taught me kattobing.

00:23:57.670 --> 00:23:59.640
Yuma seems down.

00:23:59.640 --> 00:24:04.040
He must’ve seen something
that connects this world with another world.

00:24:04.040 --> 00:24:10.010
\h\hThe Kattobing Promise\h\h

00:24:04.040 --> 00:24:07.920
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“The Kattobing Promise”

00:24:07.920 --> 00:24:10.010
Dad... Mom...

00:24:12.130 --> 00:24:14.760
The answer is...
send it to the graveyard!

00:24:14.760 --> 00:24:17.160
This is called a tribute.

00:24:17.160 --> 00:24:19.560
Tribute one monster to summon
a Level 5 or 6 monster.

00:24:19.560 --> 00:24:25.020
Tribute two monsters to summon
a Level 7-or-above monster.
